--   **Proposition 11 (power-width interchange with rows), array model.** Let the circuit satisfy the Prop. 11 hypotheses at every level (gates OK, scalar routing `ρ`, `Mout (ρ w) − Min w = 1`, every frame change `A_e` with a Lemma 10 factorization `E₁ Π_e E₂` valid mod `q ^ m ^ k`), let `s = Σ_e r_e` (`r_e` = number of ones of `Π_e`) with `s / W < m ^ τ`. Then: 1. for every `k`, the level-`k` program interchanges the two chunks of `e = m ^ k` radix-`q` digits (blockSwap of the two digit runs) whenever the row count is divisible by `W ^ k`; 2. its structural cost satisfies `T_k(V) ≤ K V (m ^ k) ^ τ`.
